{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And the land shall be forsaken by them</b> — bent zayin: for seven years sulfur and salt persisted in the Land of Israel. From the beginning of the reproof until 'their soul loathed' (Leviticus 26:43) — 90 words, corresponding to the 90 years that the ten tribes sinned, and in all of them HaShem is not mentioned, because they said: they have no portion in Elohei Yisrael. Therefore in Chronicles it is written 'and His oath to Isaac' (1 Chronicles 16:16), and in Psalms it is written 'to Isaac' (Psalm 105:9) — the Holy One, blessed be He, swore that as long as His children do not sin more than 90 years, He will not exile them. In the parashah of valuations there are 50 shekels and 30 shekels and 20 shekels and 10 shekels and 5 shekels and 3 shekels and 15 and 10 shekels between male and female, which is a total of 143 shekels, to atone for the 45 curses in the Prophets and the 98 in Mishneh Torah, which together are 143. Therefore valuations were juxtaposed to the curses."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :register {:hand-fixed {:from "the God of Israel", :to "Elohei Yisrael", :by :shovel, :date "2026-07-12"}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:25:32.725426722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}